+Files created/modified
+
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs`
+
+Verification commands and outputs
+
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`
+  - Exit code `0`
+- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::operations_tests`
+  - `9` tests passed, `0` failed
+  - Verified:
+    - `retrieve` populates selected and excluded memories
+    - `summarize` returns expected fields
+    - `filter` records predicate description
+    - `pin` is idempotent and `compress` preserves pinned identities
+    - pinned `evict` without `force` is refused
+    - forced `evict` records the caller reason
+    - `expand` adds widened candidates
+    - `checkpoint` round-trips state
+    - repeated checkpoint names version by insertion, not overwrite
+- `cd daemon && cargo build --release`
+  - Exit code `0`
+  - Output ended with: `Finished 'release' profile [optimized] target(s) in 2m 07s`
+
+Issues encountered
+
+- Initial compile failed because the new shaper detail helpers were not imported from the `retrieval_v1::shaper` module. Fixed by wiring working-memory operations to the shaper module directly.
+- `evict` initially hit a Rust borrow-checker error by mutating `excluded_memories` inside `Vec::retain`. Fixed by splitting eviction into a drain-and-rebuild helper.
+- The first test harness version incorrectly cloned the mutation observer state, so mutation records were not visible to assertions. Fixed by giving the harness stable leaked resolver storage and a shared observer reference.
+
+Final status: complete

