+
+Issues encountered
+
+- Initial compile failed because the new shaper detail helpers were not imported from the `retrieval_v1::shaper` module. Fixed by wiring working-memory operations to the shaper module directly.
+- `evict` initially hit a Rust borrow-checker error by mutating `excluded_memories` inside `Vec::retain`. Fixed by splitting eviction into a drain-and-rebuild helper.
+- The first test harness version incorrectly cloned the mutation observer state, so mutation records were not visible to assertions. Fixed by giving the harness stable leaked resolver storage and a shared observer reference.
+
+Final status: complete

codex
Implemented T35 end to end.

The working-memory operation layer now exists in [operations.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs), wired through [mod.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs), with full coverage in [operations_tests.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs). I also extended [shaper.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs) so working memory can reuse the real compression policy and recover dropped results for `excluded_memories`.

